// PORT-PENDING 1078 tests-image: tests/image.rs:1-1347
// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! U14 `.Oci` container images (D-JPK-IMAGE1=A, card c9jetpackgates, Epoch 4).
//RS //!
//RS //! `image.<name> { kind: .Oci, from: packages.<name> }` builds a deterministic,
//RS //! native OCI layout from an already-built package binary. The same record with
//RS //! `from: env.<name>` projects a verified Hangar shell output — no Docker or
//RS //! second OCI model (I6). Explicit registry pushes use the host curl adapter;
//RS //! `.Iso` disk images (the original U14 shape) ride
//RS //! the jetos installer tier (Phase D, owner-gated, untouched by this card).
//RS //!
//RS //! Covers:
//RS //!   * field-check capture through the library `evaluate_env` (kind inference,
//RS //!     `expose`/`env_vars`/`files`/`base`) — most of this lives in
//RS //!     `crates/jet-driver/src/Jetpack/ModuleEval/mod.rs`'s own unit tests;
//RS //!     this file adds the committed-fixture and cross-file-manifest angles;
//RS //!   * a library-kind (or undeclared) `from:` package is rejected (E1267);
//RS //!   * the `jetpack image <name>` engine verb: builds a real OCI layout,
//RS //!     reproducibly, from a scratch project; a `.Iso` image gets a friendly
//RS //!     "not yet" message; `--push` copies a validated local layout or uses the
//RS //!     explicit OCI Distribution HTTP(S) path, while unqualified registry
//RS //!     names remain the honest E1268 gate.
//RS 
